During a normal boot quite a lot of test is output.

The hardware consists of two controllers, and a diagnostic unit. The
terminals are connected to the controllers, not to the diagnostic unit. Each
controller has a cache, and a cache battery. I think there are variations in
how these work - there is a dual battery SSB, and single battery SSBs. I
think there may be separate caches, while ours was within the controller.

I don't know whether the controller should boot with no battery connected,
but it seems worth trying. If the battery is causing the problem, at least
that will show it.

