In article <3DCBFDFC.6A6B31E7@osfn.org>, RCS / RI <rcs@osfn.org> writes:
:
:I have a DECtalk (DTC01) that does not appear to work.  At power on
:there are a series of touch tones, and then the red LED's display
:11010010  Any hints about what this indicates would be greatly
:appreciated.

  Once the display stabilizes after powerup and self-tests and such, it
  reflects the state of the device and of the EIA232 signals that are
  visible at the DTC01.

  Assuming that LED code was not flashing and assuming that the modem
  support is disabled via SET HOST MODEM OFF, the widget looks OK -- 
  the DECtalk DTC01 is ready to or is moving data around, according 
  to the DTC01 listings I've seen.  Based on the LED display, the host
  is not asserting some typical EIA232 signals (CTS (LED0), DSR (LED2)
  and DCD (LED3), in particular) -- I'd thus check the host-side serial
  wiring and the host-side operations. 

  DECtalk is quite similar to a serial printer, in how it is accessed
  and how it is wired -- the DTC01 was typically attached to a terminal,
  then to the host system.  Having it connected to the terminal was
  handy for setup and configuration, too.

  IIRC, the signaling was usually set for 1200 baud 8N1.

  Here is a pinout for EIA232 DB25 connections commonly used with
  the DECtalk DTC01:


    TXDATA  2 ---------------   ---------------- 2 TXDATA   Transmit Data
                             \ /
                              X
                             / \
    RXDATA  3 ---------------   ---------------- 3 RXDATA   Receive Data
    
    
    RTS     4 ---------------   ---------------- 4 RTS      Request to Send
                             \ /
                              X
                             / \
    CTS     5 ---------------   ---------------- 5 CTS      Clear to Send
    
    
    DSR     6 -----+                     +------ 6 DSR      Data Set Ready is
                   |                     |                  connected to
    DCD     8 -----+---------   ---------+------ 8 DCD      Data Carrier Detect.
                             \ /
                              X
                             / \
    DTR    20 ---------------   --------------- 20 DTR      Data Terminal Ready
    
    GROUND  7 ---------------------------------- 7 GROUND   Signal Ground


  The owners of the DECtalk widgets are at http://www.fonix.com/, FWIW.

  There are various DECtalk examples and documentation and such at
  the OpenVMS Freeware website, check both the Freeware V4 and V5
  distribution directories for their (differing) contents:

    http://www.openvms.compaq.com/freeware/freeware40/dectalk/
    http://www.openvms.compaq.com/freeware/freeware50/dectalk/

