 From the OpenVMS FAQ available from http://www.openvms.compaq.com:

[FAQ]
A mirror for work performed at the Progis company in Germany in porting 
GCC (GNU C) to OpenVMS Alpha and OpenVMS VAX is available at:

     * ftp://vms.gnu.org/progis_mirror/gcc
     * http://www.levitte.org/~ava/vms_gnu.htmlx
     * ftp://ftp.caltech.edu/pub/rankin/

There are also updated header files for GCC on OpenVMS VAX that allow it 
to work with TCP/IP Sockets and the HP C RTL at:

     * ftp://ftp.qsl.net/pub/wb8tyw/gcc281_u/

The HP C compiler and other development tools are part of the OpenVMS 
Hobbyist licensing program for non-commercial users, and these and other 
tools are available to commercial developers via the CSA partner program.
[/FAQ]

The progis_mirror version is for 2.8.1 of GCC.  The most recent that I 
am aware of.  The source file for GCC.EXE appears not to match the 
binaries, and the binaries do not match the GCC CLD file, so you need to 
use foreign commands.

