  AFAICR, The "DECtalk a Guide to Voice" book was an old sales-oriented
  publication, and not particularly technically detailed.

  All of the on-line DECtalk documentation and supporting materials that 
  I have been able to locate are available on the OpenVMS Freeware -- as
  I've prised the materials loose -- and this cache has most of the 
  available technical materials, the support documentation, examples,
  and other technical stuff:

    http://www.openvms.compaq.com/freeware/freeware50/dectalk/
    http://www.openvms.compaq.com/freeware/freeware40/dectalk/

  The contents of these two directories are (quite) different!

  Most of the DECtalk materials (greatly!) pre-date the web, and were never
  particularly ported forward into HTML or other such formats.

  If there is a scanned copy of this manual around (and I don't know of 
  one), it would probably/eventually be available at the following website:

    http://www.montagar.com/~patj/dec/hcps.htm

  If you do find a copy of this sales document in the wild, please 
  let Pat (see URL above) know.

  The folks over at Fonix (http://www.fonix.com/) might well be of some
  assistance here, as well, as Fonix is where DECtalk now lives.

