,Haimo Zobernig <Haimo.Zobernig@cern.ch> said:
> We are experiencing problems in booting a few PW500au's
> running Tru64 Unix V4.0D (or F). All (ca. 8 of them) show
> exactly the same symptoms: upon the boot command, they all
> get to the point where they say "jumping to bootstrap code"
> and then they hang.
>
> Some details that may be relevant:
> We have recently moved the machines to a new location, so
> they were powered down for a few days, and now they are on
> different 100 Mb/s Ethernet connections
>
> HW: PW 500au
>     no graphics card
>     console is a VT220 terminal
>     local boot disk (scsi)
>
> SW: Tru64 Unix V4.0D or F
>     Advanced File System uses file systems on a central node
>     (a DEC 3000/300 which boots and is running)
>
> Another PW500au which does have a graphics cards seems to boot fine.
>
> Can anyone give us some hints of how to debug this? ISTR that there
> is a boot flag one can set to enable much more detailed printout
> during the boot phase, but I don't remember the flag and can't
> locate the HW manuals that should list them.
>
> Any help greatly appreciated.

At the >>> prompt check what the 'console' variable is set to?
If it is set to graphics then you will never see a login prompt on
the serial console.
If you type
set console serial
and then
init
at the >>> prompt you should see the entire boot (And indeed
it may cure the other problem).
Adam Price




